    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But why does \"being here\" matter if the person who actually lived was the one who lost everything? It feels more like I'm just stuck in an aftermath. Every day is just a repetition of a life that's already over. It’s hard to see the value in just \"breathing\" when the person who knew how to live is gone. It feels like I'm just waiting for the credits to roll on a movie that ended a long time ago.",
